# Falkensteinwand wooden stairway (one-way; top 5 px = walking surface,
# like oneway_sign): a k-outlined plank o/O with l board joints, on black
# iron knee brackets (d post + diagonal brace, m bolts, k outline) on the
# end tiles (one Y-bracket under a single tile). Transparent below, so the
# Kreuzweg's forest shows behind it; inside the shaft use steig_wall.
# Only the left/right bits change the look. No handrail: 10 px above the
# plank would be outside the 16x16 cell (see the catalog note).
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
sprite = tile_steig
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
